{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"goai-litsearch","tool":"save_to_library","arguments":{"papers_json":"[{"id":"W2064305736","title":"Stability and CMAS Resistance of Ytterbium‐Silicate/Hafnate EBCs/TBC for SiC Composites","authors":["David L. Poerschke","D. D. Hass","Susie Eustis","Gareth Seward","Jason S. Van Sluytman","Carlos G. Levi"],"year":2014,"venue":"Journal of the American Ceramic Society","doi":"10.1111/jace.13262","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/jace.13262","pdf_url":"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/pdfdirect/10.1111/jace.13262","abstract":"Multilayer ytterbium‐hafnate/silicate coatings deposited by directed vapor deposition and designed to protect SiC ‐based ceramic matrix composites were assessed to determine their thermochemical stability and resistance to attack by molten silicate deposits ( CMAS ). The study revealed that reactions occurring at the interface between Yb 2 Si 2 O 7 and Yb 4 Hf 3 O 12 layers promote coating delamination following isothermal annealing for 100 h/1500°C while coating architectures involving Yb 2 SiO 5 in contact with Yb 4 Hf 3 O 12 do not experience similar degradation. The outer Yb 4 Hf 3 O 12 layers, segmented for compliance, were only moderately effective in mitigating CMAS infiltration at 1300°C and 1500°C. The results indicate that the reaction between the melt and coating forms large volumes of a silicate garnet phase at 1300°C, or a cuspidine‐type aluminosilicate at 1500°C, in addition to the apatite and reprecipitated fluorite phases observed in related systems.","citation_count":169,"publication_type":"article","sources":["openalex"]},{"id":"W2026617778","title":"Recent progress on synthesis, multi-scale structure, and properties of Y–Si–O oxides","authors":["Ziqi Sun","Meishuan Li","Yanchun Zhou"],"year":2014,"venue":"International Materials Reviews","doi":"10.1179/1743280414y.0000000033","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1179/1743280414y.0000000033","pdf_url":"https://eprints.qut.edu.au/94599/1/Recent%20progress%20on%20synthesis%20multi-scale%20structure%20and%20properti.pdf","abstract":"Yttrium silicates (Y–Si–O oxides), including Y2Si2O7, Y2SiO5, and Y4·67(SiO4)3O apatite, have attracted wide attentions from material scientists and engineers, because of their extensive polymorphisms and important roles as grain boundary phases in improving the high-temperature mechanical/thermal properties of Si3N4 and SiC ceramics. Recent interest in these materials has been renewed by their potential applications as high-temperature structural ceramics, oxidation protective coatings, and environmental barrier coatings (EBCs). The salient properties of Y–Si–O oxides are strongly related to their unique chemical bonds and microstructure features. An in-depth understanding on the synthesis – multi-scale structure-property relationships of the Y–Si–O oxides will shine a light on their performance and potential applications. In this review, recent progress of the synthesis, multi-scale structures, and properties of the Y–Si–O oxides are summarised. First, various methods for the synthesis of Y–Si–O ceramics in the forms of powders, bulks, and thin films/coatings are reviewed. Then, the crystal structures, chemical bonds, and atomic microstructures of the polymorphs in the Y–Si–O sys …[truncated]","citation_count":144,"publication_type":"article","sources":["openalex"],"abstract_truncated":true},{"id":"W1498650167","title":"Second report on a cooperative investigation of the composition of two silicate rocks","authors":["Rollin E. Stevens","and others"],"year":1960,"venue":null,"doi":"10.3133/b1113","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.3133/b1113","pdf_url":"https://pubs.usgs.gov/bul/1113/report.pdf","abstract":"COMPOSITION OF TWO SILICATE ROCKS of these two rocks than in 1951.Improvements in previous methods and the use of new methods have given better data on major and minor elements, and new data on elements that could not be determined previously.Nevertheless, the present volun1e does not, any more than its predecessor, complete the subject.Liinited amounts of the two rocks are available to those seriously interested; requests should be addressed to the U.S. Geological Survey, Washington 25, D.C.","citation_count":81,"publication_type":"report","sources":["openalex"]},{"id":"10.1524/ncrs.2002.217.jg.25","title":"Crystal structure of the new barium zinc silicate Ba2ZnSi2O7","authors":["J. W. Kaiser","W. Jeitschko"],"year":2002,"venue":"Zeitschrift für Kristallographie - New Crystal Structures","doi":"10.1524/ncrs.2002.217.jg.25","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1524/ncrs.2002.217.jg.25","pdf_url":null,"abstract":null,"citation_count":5,"publication_type":"journal-article","sources":["crossref"]},{"id":"10.1524/ncrs.2002.217.1.25","title":"Crystal structure of the new barium zinc silicate Ba2ZnSi2O7","authors":["J. W. Kaiser","W. Jeitschko"],"year":2002,"venue":"Zeitschrift für Kristallographie - New Crystal Structures","doi":"10.1524/ncrs.2002.217.1.25","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1524/ncrs.2002.217.1.25","pdf_url":null,"abstract":null,"citation_count":4,"publication_type":"journal-article","sources":["crossref"]},{"id":"10.1016/j.displa.2017.03.001","title":"Single-phase Ce3+–Mn2+–Tb3+ tri–codoped barium–yttrium–silicate phosphors","authors":["Sangmoon Park","Sena Koh","Hyuntae Kim"],"year":2017,"venue":"Displays","doi":"10.1016/j.displa.2017.03.001","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.displa.2017.03.001","pdf_url":null,"abstract":null,"citation_count":5,"publication_type":"journal-article","sources":["crossref"]},{"id":"10.1016/b978-0-12-236306-1.50008-3","title":"Silicate Crystal Structure","authors":["WILHELM EITEL"],"year":1975,"venue":"Silicate Structures and Dispersion System","doi":"10.1016/b978-0-12-236306-1.50008-3","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/b978-0-12-236306-1.50008-3","pdf_url":null,"abstract":null,"citation_count":1,"publication_type":"book-chapter","sources":["crossref"]},{"id":"10.1016/j.matpr.2021.02.822","title":"Combustion synthesis and photoluminescence studies of rare earth activated Yttrium Barium silicate Oxyapatites","authors":["Ritu Gupta","Ananya Rout","Sadhana Agrawal"],"year":2021,"venue":"Materials Today: Proceedings","doi":"10.1016/j.matpr.2021.02.822","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.matpr.2021.02.822","pdf_url":null,"abstract":null,"citation_count":0,"publication_type":"journal-article","sources":["crossref"]}]","library_path":"<HOME>"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{
