 ${\\mathrm{Eu}}^{3+}$ in a sodium-barium-zinc silicate glass, and the temporal dependence of the emission, were measured as functions of of excitation wavelength. Large variations were observed in the intensities and wavelengths of the various components of the emission. The observed transitions were assigned in terms of a ${C}_{2v}$ site symmetry, which was found to give an adequate approximation to the symmetry of the local environment of the ion. Crystal-field calculations were performed and gave a respectable fit to the observed splitting across the entire range of pump wavelengths. A simple structural model is proposed for the behavior of the first coordination shell of the ${\\mathrm{Eu}}^{3+}$ ion in the glassy matrix. The model involves the progressive approach of a ninth ligand into an originally octacoordinate site, and is consistent with the signs and relative magnitudes of the experimentally derived crystal-field parameters.","citation_count":258,"publication_type":"article","sources":["openalex"]},{"id":"10.1016/j.jcrysgro.2018.03.040","title":"Barium and manganese-doped zinc silicate rods prepared by mesoporous template route and their luminescence property","authors":["Lingyan Dang","Chen Tian","Shifeng Zhao","Qingshan Lu"],"year":2018,"venue":"Journal of Crystal Growth","doi":"10.1016/j.jcrysgro.2018.03.040","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcrysgro.2018.03.040","pdf_url":null,"abstract":null,"citation_count":4,"publication_type":"journal-article","sources":["crossref"]},{"id":"10.1016/b978-0-12-236306-1.50008-3","title":"Silicate Crystal Structure","authors":["WILHELM EITEL"],"year":1975,"venue":"Silicate Structures and Dispersion System","doi":"10.1016/b978-0-12-236306-1.50008-3","arxiv_id":null,"url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/b978-0-12-236306-1.50008-3","pdf_url":null,"abstract":null,"citation_count":1,"publication_type":"book-chapter","sources":["crossref"]},{"id":"10.1007/s10853-020-04773-6","title":"Crystal growth velocities of 